      "title": "The Three Join Algorithms",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Three Join Algorithms",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Join Algorithm Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Join algorithm== = how rows from two inputs are matched on the condition",
                "Planner picks ==one per join node==",
                "One query can **mix** several"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Three Algorithms",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Nested Loop",
                "Hash Join",
                "Merge Join"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Method",
                  "Probe inner per outer row",
                  "Hash build side, scan probe side",
                  "Sort both, walk like zipper"
                ],
                [
                  "Condition",
                  "any",
                  "`=` only",
                  "`=` only"
                ],
                [
                  "Cost",
                  "outer rows × one inner lookup",
                  "scan each + build hash",
                  "sorts + one walk"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Hash: build on the ==smaller== input",
                "Merge: sorted output is reusable by ==ORDER BY=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Reading a Join Node",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "text",
              "lines": [
                "Hash Join",
                "  -> Seq Scan on orders",
                "  -> Hash",
                "       -> Seq Scan on users"
              ],
              "note": "outer first, inner second"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "First child = ==outer== (probe) side",
                "Second child = ==inner== (build/lookup) side"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Hash and Merge need `=`; only Nested Loop takes any condition."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "When the Planner Picks Each",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "When the Planner Picks Each",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Which Algorithm Wins",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Join",
                "Wins when",
                "Cost ≈"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:Nested Loop}",
                  "==small outer==, indexed inner column",
                  "N index lookups"
                ],
                [
                  "{blue:Hash Join}",
                  "large unsorted inputs, `=`, no useful index",
                  "one scan of each side + build hash"
                ],
                [
                  "{purple:Merge Join}",
                  "both inputs ==already sorted==, or sorted output needed",
                  "sort cost dominates if unsorted"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Conditions Limit the Choice",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`<`, `>`, `BETWEEN`, `LIKE` joins: ==Nested Loop only==",
                "`CROSS` joins: ==Nested Loop only==",
                "Hash and Merge both require an `=` condition"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Hash Join Spilling",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Hash table bigger than `work_mem` → split into ==batches== on disk",
                "`Batches > 1` in EXPLAIN means a {red:sharp slowdown}",
                "Fix: raise `work_mem` for the session, or shrink the build side"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SET work_mem = '64MB';"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "Buckets: 65536  Batches: 1  Memory Usage: 32768kB"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "Small outer + index = ==Nested Loop==. Big + `=` = ==Hash==. Sorted = ==Merge==. Anything but `=` = Nested Loop."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Join Order and Indexes That Help",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Join Order and Indexes That Help",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Join Order",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Intermediate result size== drives cost",
                "Planner joins the {green:most selective pair} first to shrink rows early",
                "Inner joins: reordered freely",
                "Reordered together up to `join_collapse_limit` / `from_collapse_limit` (default ==8==)",
                "Beyond the limit: explicit JOINs keep part of the **written order**",
                "{red:LEFT JOIN}: outer joins limit reordering, so no free swap"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Indexes That Help",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Index",
                "Enables",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "FK on inner side",
                  "Nested Loop + Index Scan",
                  "inner cost: full scan → ==lookup=="
                ],
                [
                  "Join key",
                  "Merge Join",
                  "**pre-sorted** input, no Sort"
                ],
                [
                  "`(join_col, filter_col)`",
                  "Index Only Scan",
                  "inner side skips the heap"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE INDEX ON orders (customer_id);",
                "CREATE INDEX ON orders (customer_id, status);"
              ],
              "note": "FK index, then composite for Index Only Scan"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Index the ==foreign key== used in joins. Past ==8 tables==, the written order of explicit JOINs starts to constrain the plan."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reading Joins in EXPLAIN ANALYZE",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Reading Joins in EXPLAIN ANALYZE",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Run It",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` shows ==actual== rows, time, loops beside estimates",
                "ANALYZE really **executes** the query: wrap writes in a transaction, then ROLLBACK"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)",
                "DELETE FROM orders WHERE id < 100;",
                "ROLLBACK;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Read Inside-Out",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Deepest child",
                    "sub": "runs first",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Join node",
                    "sub": "above two children",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "actual time and rows are ==per loop==: multiply by `loops`",
                "Nested Loop inner node: loops = ==outer row count==",
                "Estimated vs actual rows off by ==10x or more==: stale stats, run `ANALYZE`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Join Nodes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Node",
                "Look for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Hash Join",
                  "Hash child: Buckets, Batches, Memory Usage"
                ],
                [
                  "Merge Join",
                  "Sort children unless an index gives order"
                ],
                [
                  "Nested Loop",
                  "Seq Scan on inner side: {red:red flag}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Stale stats are the top cause of a bad join choice."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Join Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Join Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Slow Nested Loops",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No index on the ==foreign key==: inner **Seq Scan** per outer row, O(N×M)",
                "==Stale statistics== after bulk loads: rows **underestimated**",
                "Result: Nested Loop chosen where a Hash Join was needed",
                "Run `ANALYZE` after every big load"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE INDEX ON orders (customer_id);",
                "ANALYZE orders;"
              ],
              "note": "index the inner join column, refresh stats"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Index Killers",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Join condition",
                "Index used?",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`int = bigint`",
                  "{green:Yes}, cross-type operators",
                  "none needed"
                ],
                [
                  "indexed int column `= 1.5::numeric`",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "match types"
                ],
                [
                  "`a.code::int = b.id` (cast on the column)",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "match types"
                ],
                [
                  "`lower(a.x) = b.y`",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "expression index"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE INDEX ON a (lower(x));"
              ],
              "note": "expression index matches the function"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Hidden Causes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`enable_nestloop = off` in production hides the root cause",
                "Use it only to test whether another algorithm is faster",
                "Many-to-many keys across many tables multiply rows silently",
                "Check the join node's ==actual rows== against the expected count"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Fix the cause",
              "text": "Add the index, run ==ANALYZE==, match the types. Never force the plan."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Join Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Join Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pick the Algorithm",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Join",
                "Wins when",
                "Condition"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Nested Loop**",
                  "small outer + indexed inner",
                  "any (`<`, `BETWEEN`, CROSS)"
                ],
                [
                  "**Hash Join**",
                  "large inputs, no index",
                  "`=` only"
                ],
                [
                  "**Merge Join**",
                  "inputs already sorted",
                  "`=` only"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Hash spills when ==Batches > 1==",
                "Fix: raise `work_mem` for that session",
                "Or shrink the **build side**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Read the Plan",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Read **inside-out**: deepest child runs first",
                "Actual time and rows are per loop: ==multiply by loops==",
                "Estimated vs actual rows off by 10x: stale stats"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SET work_mem = '64MB';",
                "EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)",
                "SELECT * FROM orders o JOIN users u ON u.id = o.user_id;"
              ],
              "note": "ANALYZE really runs the query"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Keep Joins Cheap",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Index every ==foreign key== used in joins",
                "Run `ANALYZE` after bulk loads",
                "Keep join column types ==identical==",
                "Joins reordered together only up to `join_collapse_limit` (**8**)",
                "Outer joins limit reordering"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Red flag",
